# Env vars, secrets, and integration adapters

## Env reads only via the per-app loader (§11.5)

Each app has exactly one Zod-validated env loader. Do not read `process.env` from any other file.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — process.env read outside the env loader
const url = process.env.DATABASE_URL;

// ✅ GOOD
import { env } from '~/config/env';
const url = env.DATABASE_URL;
```

Loaders live at:
- `apps/api/src/config/env.ts`
- `apps/workers/src/config/env.ts`
- `apps/web/src/config/env.ts` (build-time, `VITE_*` only)

Loaders fail fast on boot if any required var is missing or fails its `z.string().url()` etc. validation.

## Env-var inventory (§19.19) — do not invent new names

When adding a new var, follow the existing classification:
- `[copies]` — same name as the legacy `.env`; copy across unchanged (e.g. `FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY`, `DOCUSIGN_INTEGRATION_KEY`, `OMNILIFE_USERNAME`, `SENDGRID_API_KEY`)
- `[NEW]` — new for v3; create in Doppler/Railway (e.g. `DOCUSIGN_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL`, `MICROSOFT_REDIRECT_URI`, `SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL`)
- `[v3-only]` — does not exist in legacy (Postgres, Redis, S3, observability)

`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is preferred; `CLAUDE_API_KEY` is accepted for a 30-day transition window with a deprecation warning.

## No secrets in the repo

- Doppler manages all secrets; Railway pulls from Doppler at deploy time.
- Local dev uses `doppler run -- pnpm dev`. No `.env` file with real secrets in the repo.
- The Firebase service account JSON for the API lives in Doppler as a single encrypted blob.

## All third-party integrations live behind a port (`packages/<area>/`)

Each external system has an adapter behind a stable port interface so providers can be swapped without touching feature code:

| Port | Adapters at v1 | Phase B |
|---|---|---|
| `EsignPort` | DocuSign (JWT Grant) | Adobe Sign |
| `CalendarPort` | Microsoft Graph | Google Calendar |
| `InsuranceQuotePort` | OmniLife (Basic Auth, v4.58, TAL+Zurich only) | additional sources |
| Research adapter | none at v1 (manual portfolios) | Lonsec |

Feature code calls the port; never imports a vendor SDK directly.

## OmniLife specifics (§19.12.6)

- Basic Auth (NOT bearer). API version locked to **v4.58**.
- Trial supplier set: TAL (`ACC`) and Zurich (`ZUR`). Codes outside the trial set are silently dropped; an empty resolved set falls back to all trial codes.
- Quotes cached in Redis 60 minutes keyed by canonicalised request body.
- `OMNILIFE_GROUP_ID` defaults to `'ExampleGroup'` when unset.
- The locked reference is `docs/OmniLife-API-Reference.md` — any deviation needs that doc to change first.

## DocuSign specifics (§19.12.2)

JWT Grant (server integration) — never OAuth 3-leg. Scopes `signature` + `impersonation`. Connect webhooks verified via HMAC against `DOCUSIGN_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. `DOCUSIGN_BASE_URI` is `https://demo.docusign.net` for demo and `https://www.docusign.net` for prod (helper appends `/restapi`).

## Lonsec is Phase B

No Lonsec env vars at v1. Recommended Portfolios admin is populated by hand at launch. When Lonsec goes live, the pattern is "nightly batch + local cache" — end users never call Lonsec endpoints directly.
